From 3fb9ff8c1ea24732468b034a5a2ffbc16defd446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 16:04:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] mm: route file VMA updates through shard-aware locks

hulk inclusion
category: feature
bugzilla: https://atomgit.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/9771

--------------------------------

Once a mapping is sharded, a writer must update the tree selected from the
VMA mm instead of continuing to serialize on the central i_mmap_rwsem.
The conversion race also requires a writer that found no shards to recheck
the published pointer after acquiring the central lock.

Introduce a write-lock context that records the protected tree and convert
the link, unlink, fork batch, and VMA adjustment paths. Keep the adjustment
lock from vma_prepare() through vma_complete() so readers cannot observe
a temporary remove and reinsert state.

Fork children inherit the parent mm shard selection, so lock the parent
root and keep each child immediately after its parent in interval-tree
traversal order. This preserves the rmap ordering required while
copy_page_range() copies PTEs.

Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <dongchenchen2@huawei.com>
